  "result": "Excellent! All 155 tests pass (21 new tests added). I've successfully implemented a robust date utilities module:\n\n**Created src/dates.js with three functions:**\n\n1. **isValidDate(text)** \u2014 Validates that text is a real date in YYYY-MM-DD format and interprets it as UTC. Rejects:\n   - Wrong formats (2026/01/01, 2026-1-1, etc.)\n   - Invalid dates (2026-02-30, leap year violations)\n   - Non-strings\n\n2. **addDays(date, n)** \u2014 Adds n days to a date string in UTC:\n   - Returns YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - Handles positive and negative days\n   - Crosses month and year boundaries correctly\n   - Handles leap years\n\n3. **daysBetween(a, b)** \u2014 Calculates whole days from date a to date b (UTC):\n   - Returns positive for future dates, negative for past\n   - Returns 0 for same date\n   - Inverse of addDays (addDays and daysBetween are mathematically consistent)\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- Now imports `isValidDate` from src/dates.js\n- Removed the internal isValidDate function (using centralized version)\n\n**Test Coverage (21 new tests in test/dates.test.js):**\n- Valid/invalid date formats\n- Edge cases (leap years, month/year boundaries)\n- Positive/negative day arithmetic\n- Round-trip consistency (addDays/daysBetween as inverses)\n- UTC compliance throughout\n\nAll 155 tests pass successfully!",
